# SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000077  -  CAT II
# The web server must provide install options to exclude the installation of
# documentation, sample code, example applications, and tutorials.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000077
group:           V-206377
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-000381
control_rev5:    CM-7

contribution:    Splunk delivers its tutorial content, sample dashboards, and example apps
                 as apps, each of which the application can set to a disabled state and
                 hide from the app menu, which is the strongest removal the running
                 configuration can express.

governs:         app.conf - Settings for an installed app: whether it is enabled, visible, and what it
                 may do.

check:           app.conf [install] state present
check:           app.conf [ui] is_visible present

external:        Physical removal of the sample, tutorial, and documentation app
                 directories from the installation, carried by the operating system file
                 system and the installation procedure.
external:        The installer's option set - whether the distributed package offers an
                 exclude choice and an uninstall facility - which is a property of the
                 package, not of the running configuration an assessor reads.

citation:        Web Server SRG SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000077 check and fix text;
                 app.conf.spec:124 (state), app.conf.spec:287 (is_visible)
finding:         Sample, tutorial, and documentation apps are left without a declared state
                 or visibility, so the application does not show that the example content
                 shipped with the product is disabled and out of reach.
